This cross-compilation strategy decouples language choice from deployment targets. Teams can write expressive, garbage-collected business logic that deploys either to the JVM for maximum raw throughput or to a native binary for fast startups and ultra-low memory footprints.

For systems engineers navigating container density and cloud resource costs, ahead-of-time native compilation provides a viable middle ground between manual memory management and JVM bloat.

