WavePP solves this coordination bottleneck in TensorRT-LLM by decoupling request admission from execution. Instead of blocking the pipeline, it asynchronously computes common prefix hits across all stages, locks the matching cache lines, and reserves buffer memory for remaining tokens while previous requests finish processing.

The system dynamically adjusts request chunk sizing to keep the execution pipeline saturated without starving downstream stages. Across benchmark tests on GLM and MiniMax models at concurrency 128, this asynchronous admission pipeline increased prefill throughput by factors of 2.91 and 2.02 over standard TensorRT-LLM implementations.

Decoupling cache coordination from pipeline scheduling turns fragmented cross-stage memory lookups into a predictable, non-blocking background task.

